    "notes": "Aurora because it is serverless and HP need not worry about the sudden change in workload. Elastic search for real time data monitoring. Previously used Kafka + Apache streams but lot of resources were just allocated to just manage the environment. Managed environment let them concentrate on business logic. Learning - Streaming Lambdas to DynamoDB need to be limited to 2-3 as it would throttle DynamoDB reads. Increased parallelism by leveraging 'Concurrent batches per shard feature of Lambdas'."
